What:           /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policyX/scaling_locked_limits
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        Tetris device maintainers
Description:
                Optional administrator ownership of a CPUFreq policy's software
                bounds. Frequencies use kHz. Supported on table-based drivers
                that use a target callback; other drivers return EOPNOTSUPP.

                Read: "enabled minimum maximum". When enabled is 1 the pair is
                the locked range; when 0 it is the current effective range.
                Write "1 minimum maximum" to atomically validate and apply a
                locked range. Both frequencies must be currently supported OPPs,
                minimum must not exceed maximum, and driver verification must
                preserve the pair. Invalid input changes nothing. Failed driver
                application attempts to restore the preceding lock state.
                Write "0" to release ownership and immediately apply the latest
                normal frequency-QoS aggregate. No profile is saved across reboot.

                Ordinary scaling_min_freq/scaling_max_freq writes and frequency
                QoS requests continue to update the normal requests while locked,
                but cannot change the effective policy bounds. That includes CPU
                cooling requests using frequency QoS. This interface does not
                modify the OPP table, overclock, suppress emergency shutdown, or
                disable hardware/firmware constraints. A selected bound does not
                promise an actual clock frequency under every hardware condition.

                Policy rwsem serializes sysfs operations, hotplug and policy
                refresh. Driver removal/recreation clears the lock. Ownership
                state is private to CPUFreq and does not alter the exported
                struct cpufreq_policy ABI.
